course: dictionary
lesson: 494
title: Place words in names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. «Asiatic» means from Asia. «A small group of Asiatic lions lives in India's Gir Forest.» India is in Asia, so the word tells you where these lions come from.
explain: Look at the words next to it. «The Asiatic black bear, or moon bear, has a cream-coloured crescent on its chest.» Asiatic is part of the bear's name, like a label. It is used mostly for names of animals and plants, not for describing people.
explain: Be careful with people. «Asiatic» about people is old-fashioned and many find it offensive, so today we say «Asian». Check with the swap test: put «Asian» in place of the word in a sentence about people, and see if it still makes sense and sounds respectful.
fact: «Asiatic» means from Asia.
fact: It is mostly used in names of animals and plants, such as «Asiatic lion» and «Asiatic black bear».
fact: About people, «Asiatic» is old-fashioned and can offend; say «Asian» instead.
fact: «The Asiatic black bear» lives in forests from Afghanistan to Japan, and has a cream-coloured crescent on its chest.
fact: A small group of Asiatic lions lives in India's Gir Forest.
exercise: «A small group of Asiatic lions lives in India's Gir Forest.» What does Asiatic mean here? | Very large and fierce | Made of stone | *From Asia | Living in deserts
exercise: The Asiatic black bear lives in forests from Afghanistan to Japan. Where is that? | *Asia | Australia | Antarctica | Africa
exercise: Lily says her grandma is «Asiatic». Why should she not use that word for people? | *It is old-fashioned and can offend | It is only used for lions | It is too long | Grandma is not from Asia
test: «Wild lions now live mainly in parts of Africa, and Asiatic lions only in and around Gir Forest in India.» Where do Asiatic lions live in the wild? | Savanna in Africa | *Gir Forest in India | A jungle in Brazil | The deserts of Australia
test: «Asiatic cheetah» is a name for an animal. What is the best way to check what Asiatic means? | Guess it is a colour | Ignore it, because names don't matter | Use it for people, as it is the same as Asian | *Swap in «from Asia» and see if it makes sense
exam: What does the word Asiatic in «Asiatic black bear» tell you? | It means the bear is very big | *It comes from Asia | It means the bear lives in a zoo | It is the bear's favourite food
